  "slug": "coherent-unitary-6215",
  "summary": "Recent preprints extend programmable unitary photonic circuits to on-chip interconnects, optical neural networks, modular processors, and spectral measurement.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is the use of programmable unitary interferometric circuits as the computational or functional primitive in coherent photonic systems. The preprint 2611.20390 proposes a logarithmic-depth butterfly interferometer architecture for parameter-efficient unitary transformations in coherent optical neural networks, while 2611.21582 builds a modular processor from unitary tiles of fixed mixers and programmable phases, evaluated by numerical fitting. The silicon chip in 2611.23667 uses unequal path lengths between two 8x8 unitary circuits to perform simultaneous spectral measurement and programmable filtering at 0.05 nm resolution. The coherent-lite interconnect in 2611.19254, which combines wavelength and mode multiplexing with self-homodyne detection, is a related on-chip coherent link reaching 103.96 Tb/s aggregate line rate. What is new is the joint emphasis on depth-efficient parameterization, modular tiling of unitary elements, and multifunctional use across computation, measurement, and interconnection.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-23"
}
